WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.150
The Pokémon World Championships,
Hyper Class...

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:12.080
After claiming victory in his battle
with Mary at Galar’s Shoot Stadium,

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.870
Satoshi stayed the night
at the Pokémon Center with Go, but...

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.060
Morning, Pikachu...

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:36.980
Huh?

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.060
Where’s Go?

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.240
You wouldn’t wake up no matter how hard I tried,
so I’m going on ahead to Engine Riverside!

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.820
Come find me when you wake up!

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.320
Ahh...

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.910
I promised him we were gonna wake up early
and look for Galar Pokémon...

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.700
Let’s hurry after him, Pikachu!

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.160
Erm...

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.460
To get to Engine Riverside,
I take the train to Engine City...

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.960
Hurry up!
Mr. Dande’s battle started already!

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:07.840
I know!

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.840
Huh? Mr. Dande’s battle?!

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.010
H-H-H—

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.470
Hold on!

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.350
Whoa!
You beat Mary yesterday!

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.810
We watched your battle!
You’re really strong!

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.100
Thanks!

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.690
But forget that,
where’s Mr. Dande?!

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.770
Oh, Mr. Dande should be at
Shoot Stadium right now—

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:24.860
Really?!

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.070
I wanna watch!

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.570
He’s so fast...

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:10.670
Please!

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.920
Don’t let me be too late!

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.970
What a fierce showdown!

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.810
Now <i>this</i> is a Master Class battle!

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:28.270
Will the 7th-place Competitor Ohba be able to take down
the 1st-place Competitor Dande’s bastion of power?!

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:34.070
So he’s facing Mr. Ohba
from the Sinnoh Elite Four?!

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.570
No, gotta hurry!

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.080
Dragon Claw!

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:48.330
Dodge it!

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.250
Flare Drive!

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:54.300
An interesting choice.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.210
We’ll face it head on!

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.680
Lizardon, use Flare Drive!

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:07.810
Circle around
and use Mach Punch!

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.110
Flamethrower!

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:15.490
What?!

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:16.780
Dragon Claw!

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.790
Goukazaru is unable to battle!
Lizardon wins!

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.540
As such, the winner is
Competitor Dande!

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.220
An absolute Monarch!
Absolutely the strongest!

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:44.350
Champion Dande has added
a new page to his undefeated legend!

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.350
Based on the results of this battle,

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:51.190
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.780
You tried your hardest.

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:58.990
Return, Goukazaru.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.250
I expected no less, Champion.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.750
Let’s have another
heated battle sometime!

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.550
He really is amazing!

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:22.130
Man, Mr. Dande was so cool...

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.970
Wish I could’ve seen
the whole thing.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.350
What’s that?

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.350
Mr. Dande!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.350
Congratulations, Mr. Dande!

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.150
So cool!

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:34.360
Thank you.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.360
Thank you, all of you!

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.940
He’s so popular...

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.360
He <i>is</i> the unbeatable Champion,
after all...

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.120
Look forward to my next battle,
everyone!

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.200
Mr. Dande!

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.870
Oh, if it isn’t Satoshi!

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.410
Did you see my battle?

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.210
Yeah!

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.920
I had a battle here yesterday...

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.040
...and I won!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.300
15th, huh?

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.550
You’re nearly at the heels
of the Master Class.

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:01.420
Yeah!

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:02.800
Oh, right, Satoshi.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.300
Are you free now?

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.680
I’m about to head out for some training.
Wanna come with me?

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.390
Training?

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.350
After having just battled?

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.310
Lizardon and I
haven’t had enough fun just yet.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.060
Count me in!

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.450
They look like they’re having fun.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.460
Okay, that’s it!

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.550
Himenka’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.180
All right!
I caught a Himenka!

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:54.810
Nice to meet you!

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.900
Himenka! Flowering Pokémon!
Grass type!

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:04.450
It anchors itself in the ground with its single leg,
and its flower takes on color as it sings a joyous song!

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:08.410
But...
Satoshi’s sure taking his time.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:11.080
Don’t tell me he’s still sleeping...

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.830
Calling! Calling!

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:15.500
Oh, Go?

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:17.830
Satoshi!
What are you doing?!

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.250
I’ve been waiting for you!

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.380
Oh, sorry, I forgot.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.090
Huh?!

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:25.220
I’m going training
with Mr. Dande right now!

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:26.840
Mr. Dande?!

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:27.640
How?

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:28.720
Stuff happened.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:31.060
So I’ll meet up with you later.

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:32.600
Okay.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:35.940
Let’s meet back at
the Pokémon Center in 3 hours, then.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:40.110
I would have liked
to see Mr. Dande, too...

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:45.070
Okay! I’ll have to make up for it
by catching lots of rare Pokémon!

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.610
Go, is that you?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.740
Ms. Sonia?!

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.200
What brings you here?

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.830
Fieldwork.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.960
I’ve been surveying the Power Spots
in the Wild Area.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:02.090
What about you, though?
What brings you here?

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:04.510
I thought I’d catch some
Galar Pokémon.

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:06.340
Is that so?

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:09.510
There’s a spot with
plenty of Pokémon right nearby.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:10.260
Want me to take you?

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.010
Uh... What, in your car?

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:15.390
D-Don’t worry,
I can get there fine on my ow—

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.230
You don’t have to be so coy!

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:20.060
We’re pals who’ve
researched legends together!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.020
Go on, go on!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:22.150
No, wait...!

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:26.400
Oh, Go’s in Galar with you?
I should have invited him too, then.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:29.240
Oh, he’s knee deep in
catching Pokémon right now.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:32.320
By the way,
where are you gonna train?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.040
The sea!

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.200
The sea, huh?!

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:46.960
Huh?

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.880
Um...
Where’s the sea?

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:56.020
Satoshi!
Today, I’m going to train in the mountains!

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:00.020
Uh... But you said
the sea before...

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:01.980
Don’t tell me
you got lost...?

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:03.770
Don’t get caught up
in the details!

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:05.900
Let’s have fun!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.190
R-Right!

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:10.200
This looks like a good spot.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.200
Lizardon!

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:19.750
Come on, Satoshi!

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:20.410
Right!

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.670
Make sure you hold on tight!

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.090
Here we go!

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:29.050
Go straight ahead, Lizardon!

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:31.130
Dodge!

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.430
Isn’t this thrilling?

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.180
It’s just like Sonia’s driving!

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:49.360
I see, so Satoshi’s
with Dande right now.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.360
He mentioned...

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:52.860
Ow!

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.320
Something...

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.410
About training...

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.580
I think...

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:58.990
Huh.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.040
Well, I hope they didn’t go
anywhere too weird.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:02.790
Huh?

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:06.630
Dande’s <i>horrifyingly</i> bad
with directions.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:09.050
Huh? He is?

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:13.510
I can’t think of a single time he made it
from one place to another without incident.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:14.970
Huh...

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:17.760
I thought he was supposed to be
this perfect Champion...

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:23.060
Well, he’s great at battles,
and he is the undefeated Champion...

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:29.190
But he’s nothing like the public image
he has of being this charismatic figure, this big hero.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.190
Is that right?

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.030
Oh, over there!

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.490
Dragon Claw!

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.250
Awesome!

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:55.760
Okay, Lizardon!
Next, we’ll do that!

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:57.550
We’re going under, Satoshi!

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:07.980
That was amazing!
The best!

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.320
Satoshi, do you like skydiving?

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:12.440
Huh?

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.320
Return, Lizardon!

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.490
Drapult!

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:30.040
Nice catch!

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:34.720
Is this how you train every day,
Mr. Dande?!

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:36.300
Yeah! Isn’t it fun?

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.140
It’s super fun!

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:41.970
Some Wooloo!

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:44.980
There’s loads of them!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.020
Descend, Drapult!

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:07.000
That tickles!

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.330
We’ve already made
some new friends!

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:11.460
What do you think?

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.920
Doesn’t it look like
it’s teeming with Pokémon?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.050
I’ll help you too,
so try your best to catch them!

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:18.380
Wait...

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.680
What happened?

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:22.510
Oh, uh...
Nothing.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.640
Pull yourself together...

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:29.900
You’ve got to catch lots of Pokémon,
so you can brag to Satoshi and Dande!

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:30.900
Right.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:33.440
Oh, right, Ms. Sonia.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:37.240
You said Mr. Dande’s nothing
like his heroic image before.

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:39.030
What is he really like, then?

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.740
Good point...

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:46.410
He’s like this big kid... A Pokémon freak
who can’t sit still whenever he sees a Pokémon!

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.540
A kid who’s a Pokémon freak...

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:50.870
That’s basically Satoshi!

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.540
Ahh, they’re so fluffy...

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:56.630
Yeah, they’re so fluffy...

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:13.900
Drameshiya!

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:16.400
Hey! Wait for us!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.360
Let’s play together!

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.320
You know, Dande...

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.030
When he was young,
he didn’t have many friends.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.830
Huh? Really?

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:28.790
He was probably too busy helping out around
the house, and taking care of his little brother,

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:31.830
and didn’t get to play
with kids of his age much.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.170
He’d sometimes spend time with me,
his childhood friend, but that’s all.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:36.840
But then...

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.010
One day, he met a Hitokage.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:43.430
Ever since he learned
how to battle with Pokémon,

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:47.890
he’s been surrounded by so many people,
friends and rivals alike.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:49.730
Yes...

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:53.690
Pokémon really have
expanded his world.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.160
I was hungry,
so this tastes great!

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:05.660
Yeah, it’s great!

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:07.910
We got in some
great training today!

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:09.370
That was training?

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:10.540
Yeah.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:12.750
Battling, training, playing...

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:14.670
They’re all the same to me.

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:17.000
Getting some exercise
with Pokémon...

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.630
It’s just plain fun!

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:20.880
I really know how you feel!

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:23.930
And I knew you’d say that!

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:29.470
Vast skies, great food,
Pokémon by your side...

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:30.890
It doesn’t get better than this!

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:31.850
Yeah!

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.480
What’s that?!

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.320
Pocket Monsters!

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:55.750
Armorgaw. Raven Pokémon.
Flying/Steel type.

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.250
It reigns supreme in the skies
of the Galar region.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:02.510
The black luster of its steel body
could drive terror into the heart of any foe.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.760
Something’s strange about this.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:17.900
The Drameshiya
and Wooloo!

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:20.980
Those Armorgaw seem
unusually agitated.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:25.360
This isn’t good. We have to
do something, or they’ll get hurt!

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.490
Let’s go, Drapult!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:28.490
You’re gonna battle them?

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.490
If I need to!

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:31.990
Let’s lure them away,
one at a time!

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.420
Come on, this way!

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:39.790
That’s it! Follow me!

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.760
You still wanna run riot
some more, huh?

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:47.180
Then I’ll be your playmate!

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:48.510
Drapult, go!

00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:00.150
Can you catch up to my Drapult?

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:05.030
What’s Mr. Dande going to do?

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:09.530
I wonder why the Armorgaw
attacked the Drameshiya...

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:13.660
It was like they tried
to drive them away from the cliff...

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:28.930
Too slow!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.140
Is there something up there?

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.230
All right!

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:42.190
You have me trapped, huh?

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:43.770
Drapult, let’s break through!

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:47.070
Dodge!

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:50.950
Return, Drapult!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.540
Man, you’re full of energy!

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:02.710
Whoa, that’s awesome!

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.500
Oh, right.

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:10.430
That should be about enough.

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:16.600
Have you calmed down?

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.810
Don’t worry, I’m no enemy.

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:21.140
Now, let’s fly together!

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:35.370
Kokogara. Tiny Bird Pokémon.
Flying type.

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:38.910
It will face any opponent with its small body,
no matter their size.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:41.420
Armorgaw is its final evolution.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:43.830
It’s hurt?!

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:47.210
So the Armorgaw
were protecting these chicks...

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.800
I’ve gotta tell Mr. Dande!

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:55.350
Hey, stop!
Stay away from there!

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:00.180
What?

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:00.980
Hey! Stop!

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:18.620
Satoshi!

00:18:24.210 --> 00:18:25.750
Mr. Dande!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:26.630
Huh?

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:30.960
I see, so the Armorgaw
were protecting these chicks...

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:37.260
All right, that should do it.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:39.060
Be careful, okay?

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.030
We did it.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.960
That mid-air catch was so reckless...

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:15.590
I just can’t hold back
when it comes to Pokémon...

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.930
I’d have probably done
the same thing.

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.060
Mr. Dande...

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:23.980
What’s it like to be Champion?

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:28.440
For so long, I was afraid...

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:32.570
I’ve never lost a Pokémon battle.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.360
And it scared me.

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:42.040
Maybe it meant I’d reached my limit,
and couldn’t improve any further...

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:45.540
Maybe I could never get any stronger...

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:50.250
But back then...

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.340
The sky!

00:19:57.930 --> 00:20:01.430
Is this Mugendaina?!

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:14.280
I was utterly helpless
against Mugendaina.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:23.290
It frustrated me...
But it also thrilled me.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:27.750
Finding out there’s still guys
who are stronger than me!

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:29.920
And I can chase after them!

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:33.500
I really can get stronger!

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:38.720
I... I think I like you
even more now, Mr. Dande!

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:42.550
And now I wanna beat you
even more than before!

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:48.850
Hurry up and reach me, Satoshi!

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:49.520
Right!

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:54.110
Now then,
should we make our way back?

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:56.280
Pikachu! We’re leaving!

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.620
By the way...

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:07.200
Any idea where I left my car?

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.910
What?!

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:24.100
Sorry for the wait, Go.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:25.350
Honestly...

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:26.640
You’re <i>very</i> late!

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:27.720
Sorry, sorry...

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:30.480
Oh boy,
I sure got lost out there...

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:32.230
I knew you would.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:37.480
Spending time with Dande has made Satoshi
look forward to their battle even more.

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:41.030
When will they battle over the
title of the strongest?

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.580
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.750 --> 00:23:12.700
What’s that?

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:15.920
Bacchinkey!
The evolved form of Sarunori!

00:23:15.920 --> 00:23:19.170
But he only has one stick...

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:21.130
Is there something
we can do for him?

00:23:21.130 --> 00:23:23.470
If we could find a stick that fits...

00:23:23.470 --> 00:23:27.590
Even if it fits,
they want a certain feel...

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:29.850
They’re picky with their sticks.

00:23:29.850 --> 00:23:31.680
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:34.230
The One Stick Bacchinkey!
